{
  "name": "history-fixed-to-week-based-no-transition",
  "description": "A change without a transition from calendar years (fixed_date, 1 January) to ISO 8601-style week years (week_based, Monday nearest 1 January) from 2024-01-01, a Monday that is a year boundary of both rules. Numbered by 'majority', the years are consecutive. Weeks of 2023 follow the fixed-date rule (week 1 is Sunday 1 January 2023 alone, weeks are LEVEL_NOT_NESTED in its quarters, a week's parent is the year); from 2024 weeks are whole and nest in periods. The week years from 2024 agree with Python's date.isocalendar() (asserted by the generator). Illustrative.",
  "source": {
    "kind": "oracle",
    "citation": "Independent implementation of the spec in conformance/generators/fiscal_oracle.py, written with Python datetime and no fiscalclock code",
    "url": null,
    "checked_by": "fiscal_oracle.py: Calendar.seq built from the regimes and transitions; change_errors and naming_errors pass; ISO years checked against date.isocalendar()"
  },
